          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon C \to D
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %strong final
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagrams"} diagrams
            along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            does not change their
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
          %p
            Dually, a functor is
            %strong initial
            if pulling back diagrams along it does not change the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            of these diagrams.
          %p
            Beware that this property is pretty much unrelated to that of a functor being an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,D]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\in D
            is initial (resp. terminal) just when the corresponding functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \colon 1\to D
            is initial (resp. final).
          %p
          #WarningOnTerminology.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (warning on terminology)
              %br/
              In older references (and also some others like
              = succeed ")," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT
              = succeed "," do
                %em cofinal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/order+theory"} order theory
              (cf.
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofinality"} cofinality
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
              because usually the prefix “co-” denotes
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} dualization
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#fb"} Borceux
              %em dual
              concept, but in general it seems that the consensus is to use “final” for what used to be called “cofinal”, and “initial” for the dual concept (since “co-final” would be ambiguous). For example,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"} Johnstone
              in
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant"} Sketches of an Elephant
              says (before Proposition B2.5.12 ):
            %blockquote
              %p Traditionally, final functors were called ‘cofinal functors’; but this use of ‘co’ is potentially misleading as it has nothing to do with dualization — it is derived from the Latin ‘cum’ rather than ‘contra’ — and so it is now generally omitted.
            %p
              See also the warning at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/final+%28infinity%2C1%29-functor"}
                  final
                  = succeed "-functor" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              (
              %a{:href => "final+infinity1-functor#CofinalTerminologyWarning"}> here
              ).
          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to D
              is
              %strong final
              if for every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in D
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d/F)
              is (non-empty and)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+category"} connected
              (the non-emptiness condition is redundant since connected categories are non-empty by convention).
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to D
              is
              %strong initial
              if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mi op
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{op} : C^{op} \to D^{op}
              is final, i.e. if for every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in D
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F/d)
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+category"} connected
          %h2#properties Properties
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to D
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %p The following conditions are equivalent.
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  is final.
              %li#AnItem
                %p
                  For all functors
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mo :
                        %mi D
                        %mo →
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G : D \to Set
                  the natural
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                  between
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                        %mi G
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi F
                        %mo →
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\lim_\to G \circ F \to \lim_{\to} G
                %p
                  is a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              %li
                %p
                  For all categories
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  and all functors
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mo :
                        %mi D
                        %mo →
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G : D \to E
                  the natural
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                  between
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                        %mi G
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi F
                        %mo →
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\lim_\to G \circ F \to \lim_{\to} G
                %p
                  is an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %li
                %p
                  For all functors
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mo :
                        %msup
                          %mi D
                          %mi op
                        %mo →
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G : D^{op} \to Set
                  the natural
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                  between
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ←
                        %mi G
                        %mo →
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ←
                        %mi G
                        %mo ∘
                        %msup
                          %mi F
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\lim_\leftarrow G \to \lim_\leftarrow G \circ F^{op}
                %p
                  is a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              %li
                %p
                  For all categories
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  and all functors
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mo :
                        %msup
                          %mi D
                          %mi op
                        %mo →
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G : D^{op} \to E
                  the natural
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ←
                        %mi G
                        %mo →
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ←
                        %mi G
                        %mo ∘
                        %msup
                          %mi F
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\lim_\leftarrow G \to \lim_\leftarrow G \circ F^{op}
                %p
                  is an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %li
                %p
                  For all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in D
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mi c
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi C
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mo *
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        {\lim_\to}_{c \in C} Hom_D(d,F(c)) \simeq *
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  for all functors
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                          %mo :
                          %mi D
                          %mo →
                          %mi E
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G: D \to E
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Nat
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi Nat
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi GF
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mi E
                        %mo →
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Nat(G,\Delta-)\to Nat(GF,\Delta-) : E \to Set
                %p
                  between the functors of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocones"} cocones
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi GF
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GF
                  is an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                  = succeed "\u2018s" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Δ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Nat
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Nat
                  stands for the set of natural transformations.)
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#KashiwaraSchapira06"}> Kashiwara &amp; Schapira 2006, Prop. 2.5.2
            )
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to D
              is final then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is connected precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              is.
          #Stability.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_2
              are final, then so is their composite
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_1 \circ F_2
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_2
              and the composite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_1 \circ F_2
              are final, then so is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_1
            %p
              Final functors are stable under
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              of final functors in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Cat
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Cat}^{\mathbf{2}}
              is a final functor.
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_1
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
              and the composite is final, then both functors seperately are final.
          %p
            The first two statements of Proposition
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Stability"}
            in fact follow from the stability properties of orthogonal factorization systems:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              Final functors and
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/discrete+fibration"} discrete fibrations
              form an
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/orthogonal+factorization+system"} orthogonal factorization system
              called the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comprehensive+factorization+system"} comprehensive factorization system
          %h2#generalizations Generalizations
          %h3#exact_squares Exact squares
          %p
            The characterization of final functors is a special case of the characterization of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+squares"} exact squares
          %h3#FinalityForWeightedLimits Final enriched functors
          %p
            Finality for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functors"} enriched functors
            with respect to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+colimits"} weighted colimits
            (for enrichment in a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#Kelly82"} Kelly 1982 §4.5
          %p
            See also discussion of finality specifically for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coends"} coends
            (initiality for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limits"} weighted limits
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ends"} ends
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Campion"}> Tim Campion
              \:
              %em Cofinality for Coends
              (2020) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/q/353876/381"}> MO:q/353876
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/354097/381"} MO:a/354097
          %h3#final_functors
            Final
            = succeed "-functors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            The generalization of the notion of final functor from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            to
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            is described at
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/final+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"}> final (∞,1)-functor
              \.
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %p
          #InclusionOfATerminalObjectIsFinal.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} inclusion
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                is
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/final+functor"} final functor
              %br/
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              then the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : {*} \to D
              that picks that terminal object is final: for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in D
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d/F
              is equivalent to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *\to D
              is final, then its image is a terminal object.
            %p
              In this case the statement about preservation of colimits states that the colimit over a category with a terminal object is the value of the diagram at that object. Which is also readily checked directly.
              %br/
          %p
            More generally (see Lemma 3.7 of
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#Clarke2024"} Clarke 2024
          %p
          .num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              A functor whose domain is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+category"} discrete category
              is final if and only if it is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful"} fully faithful
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              That every right adjoint functor is final is proven below. For the converse, suppose that we have a final functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to D
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is discrete. Finality says that, for each
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in D
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \downarrow F
              is connected: - Nonemptyness of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \downarrow F
              says that there exists some
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_d \in C
              and morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi d
                    %mo :
                    %mi d
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_d : d \to F(c_d)
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c, c' \in C
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ←
                      %mi d
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(c) \leftarrow d \rightarrow F(c')
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo =
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c = c'
              and that the two legs are equal.
            %p
              Consequently, we have an assignment
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |D| \to |C|
              sending
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ↦
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \mapsto c_d
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi d
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo ,
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(c_d, c') \cong D(d, R(c'))
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is discrete, this says that there exists at most one morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \to R(c')
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi d
                      %mo =
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_d = c'
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi d
                      %mo =
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_d = c'
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_d
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \to R(c')
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c' = c_d
              by the path existence property.
            %p
              Full faithfulness now follows, since
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Fc
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Fc
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi Fc
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(Fc, Fc') \cong C(c_{Fc}, c') = C(c, c')
          %p
          #FinalFunctorBetweenGroupoids.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              A functor between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
              is final iff it is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+functor"} full
          (eg.
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#Cigoli18"} Cigoli 2018, Prop. 1.1
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
              is final.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R) : C \to D
              be a pair of
              = succeed ".To" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is final, we may for instance check that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in D
              the comma category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d / R
              is non-empty and connected:
            %p
              It is non-empty because it contains the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} adjunction unit
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi d
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L(d), d \to R L (d))
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi g
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; d
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{f}}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{g}}
                    \\\
                    R(a) &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; R(b)
                    }
            %p
              two objects, they are connected by a zig-zag going through the unit, by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor#UniversalArrows"} universal factorization property
              of adjunctions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ←
                              %mrow
                                %mi R
                                %mover
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi R
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mover
                                  %mi g
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; d
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \swarrow &amp;\downarrow&amp; \searrow
                    \\\
                    R(a) &amp;\stackrel{R \bar f}{\leftarrow}&amp; R L (d)&amp; \stackrel{R(\bar g)}{\to} &amp; R(b)
                    }
                    \\,.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              The inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} \to \tilde \mathcal{C}
              of any category into its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+completion"} idempotent completion
              is final.
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+completion"} idempotent completion
            in the section on
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Karoubi+envelope#Finality"} Finality
          #CoconeUnderCospan.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              The inclusion of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospan
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              into its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
