          #FiberProductsInASliceCategory.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              By the characterization (
              %a{:href => "overcategory#LimitsInSliceViaLimitsOfCoconedDiagram"}> here
              ) of limits in a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+products"} fiber products
              in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
              are computed as fiber products in the underlying category, or in other words that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
              to the point preserves fiber products.
          %p
          #FirstPairOfFaceMapsFinalInOppositeSimplexCategory.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^{op}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
              of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              inclusion of the lowest two face maps
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big(
                    [1]
                    \\underoverset
                    {d_0}
                    {d_1}
                    {\rightrightarrows}
                    [0]
                    \\big)
                    \\;\xrightarrow{\;\;\;\;}\;
                    \\Delta^{op}
            %p is a final functor.
            %p
              It follows that the
